## Layout

### Grid

- Max content width: 1440px. Internal content max: 1280px with auto margins.
- Twelve column base, but layouts use asymmetric splits often: 60/40, 70/30, 40/60.
- Gutters: 24px minimum, 40px preferred.
- Section rhythm: 80px minimum between sections, 120px to 160px preferred on desktop.

### Container queries are the component responsiveness primitive

This is the second large change for 2026. A component should respond to the space it sits in, not to the viewport. A feature card in a wide hero and the same card in a narrow sidebar should adapt themselves, with no viewport breakpoint guessing which context they are in. Mark a wrapper as a container and query it:

```css
.card-frame { container-type: inline-size; container-name: card; }

@container card (min-width: 30rem) {
  .card { grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr; }
}
```

Viewport breakpoints still set the page frame and the major column splits. Container queries handle everything reusable. Build new components container query first, and the mobile pass becomes far smaller.

### Subgrid for editorial alignment

When grid items contain their own rows (image, then headline, then caption) and those rows must line up across a mosaic or a magazine spread, use `subgrid` so the inner rows inherit the parent tracks. It removes the fragile fixed heights that used to force alignment:

```css
.mosaic { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(12, 1fr); }
.mosaic-item { display: grid; grid-template-rows: subgrid; grid-row: span 3; }
```

### Canonical layout patterns

Use these. Do not invent generic ones.

- **Split hero 60/40 or 70/30.** Full viewport height (`min-h-dvh`). Left: display text and a single CTA. Right: full bleed photography. No card, no box, no border. The image is the right half of the viewport.
- **Editorial stack.** Full width image, display headline overlapping the bottom of the image, body below on white. The image bleeds edge to edge.
- **Image mosaic.** Asymmetric grid of three to five images at different sizes. One dominates. No equal thumbnails. Gap 8px to 12px. No rounded corners. Subgrid for caption alignment.
- **Magazine spread.** Two columns mimicking print. Left: a large number or display word as structure. Right: photography and caption. Or invert.
- **Product or feature grid.** Four columns on desktop, two on mobile, but vary weight rather than tiling uniform cards. Image above, minimal label below. No border, no shadow. Hover scales the image to 1.02 only.
- **Stat or pull quote block.** Full width near black section. A large number or short quote at display scale. Small caption. One thin rule above and below. No icons.

