## Structural details

### Thin rule lines

1px lines in `#E0DED8` or `rgba(0,0,0,0.10)` to separate nav items, frame a section with a top rule only (not a box), divide caption from image, or structure multi column text. Never a decorative border around a component.

### Rotated and sideways text

For vertical section labels along a left edge, category indicators, or column identifiers. Hidden on mobile (see the mobile document).

```css
.sidebar-label {
  writing-mode: vertical-rl;
  text-orientation: mixed;
  transform: rotate(180deg);
  font-size: 11px;
  letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--color-text-secondary);
}
```

### Arrows

Arrows are functional navigation and direction, never decoration. Use them for next section indicators, CTA links (the arrow replaces "click here"), carousel controls, pagination, and breadcrumb separators. Thin SVG or CSS drawn, never emoji, never an icon library glyph, never a fat chevron or a filled head.

```tsx
// components/ui/Arrow.tsx
export const Arrow = ({ direction = 'right' }: { direction?: 'right' | 'left' | 'down' }) => (
  <svg width="32" height="12" viewBox="0 0 32 12" fill="none"
       stroke="currentColor" strokeWidth="1" aria-hidden="true">
    {direction === 'right' && (<><line x1="0" y1="6" x2="30" y2="6" /><polyline points="24,1 30,6 24,11" /></>)}
    {direction === 'left'  && (<><line x1="32" y1="6" x2="2" y2="6" /><polyline points="8,1 2,6 8,11" /></>)}
    {direction === 'down'  && (<><line x1="16" y1="0" x2="16" y2="10" /><polyline points="11,5 16,11 21,5" /></>)}
  </svg>
)
```

```tsx
<a className="cta-link">View all services <Arrow direction="right" /></a>
```

