## Theme tokens, Tailwind v4 CSS first

All tokens live in one `@theme` block in the global stylesheet. Tailwind v4 generates the matching utilities automatically (`--color-accent` becomes `bg-accent` and `text-accent`, `--spacing-section` becomes `py-section`) and the variables are also plain CSS variables everywhere.

```css
/* globals.css */
@import "tailwindcss";

:root { color-scheme: light dark; }

@theme {
  /* Brand colors, replace with client values */
  --color-background: light-dark(#F5F4F0, #0A0A0A);
  --color-text: light-dark(#1A1A1A, #F2F1EC);
  --color-text-secondary: oklch(0.55 0 0);
  --color-accent: /* brand accent in oklch */;
  --color-rule: light-dark(#E0DED8, rgba(255,255,255,0.14));

  /* Spacing */
  --spacing-sm: 16px;
  --spacing-md: 24px;
  --spacing-lg: 40px;
  --spacing-xl: 64px;
  --spacing-2xl: 96px;
  --spacing-section: clamp(80px, 10vw, 160px);

  /* Fluid type scale */
  --text-display: clamp(64px, 10vw, 160px);
  --text-display--line-height: 1.0;
  --text-h1: clamp(40px, 6vw, 96px);
  --text-h1--line-height: 1.1;
  --text-h2: clamp(24px, 3.5vw, 48px);
  --text-h2--line-height: 1.2;

  /* Fonts, wired to next/font variables */
  --font-display: var(--font-display), system-ui, sans-serif;
  --font-body: var(--font-body), system-ui, sans-serif;
}
```

A v3 project keeps `tailwind.config.ts` with `theme.extend`. Do not mix the two systems. The target state is everything in `@theme`.

