## The AI giveaways, never ship these

A site built well under this system is unidentifiable as machine assisted. The copy rules handle the writing tells. These are the visual tells that mark a page as AI generated, and every one is banned:

- **Purple to blue or indigo to violet gradients.** The default startup builder hero. No gradients exist in this system at all, so it is already covered, but it is the single most common tell, so it is named first and explicitly.
- **Gradient text.** A headline is a solid color, never a clipped gradient fill.
- **Glassmorphism.** No frosted translucent cards, no backdrop blur panels floating over a busy background.
- **Mesh, aurora, or blob backgrounds.** No soft colored orbs drifting behind content.
- **Bento grids of uniform rounded cards.** Vary size and weight, square the corners, let photography and type carry the structure.
- **The generic three column feature row:** an icon, a heading, one line, repeated three times. If features are shown they are editorial, asymmetric, and photography led.
- **Sparkle or star AI icons, gradient pills, glow effects.** None.
- **Centered everything:** a centered hero with a centered eyebrow, centered subhead, and a centered button. The house aesthetic is left aligned and asymmetric.
- **Default shadcn, Chakra, or Material shipped unrestyled.** The primitives are fine. The default skin is a tell.
- **Emoji anywhere in the UI.**
- **Rounded corners on everything.** Radius is 0 to 4px, never the soft 12 to 24px that templates default to.
- **Glowing or colored shadows.** Shadows are near absent and never tinted.

The test: if a screenshot of the page could be mistaken for a generic template or an AI builder's default output, it has failed. The page reads as a designed editorial object with a point of view, or it is not done.

---

## What to never do

- No gradients, anywhere.
- No colored drop shadows.
- No radius above 4px on editorial elements (buttons 2px max, inputs 0).
- No uniform equal size card grids. Vary size and weight.
- No stock illustration or icon heavy UI.
- No centered body text.
- No hyphens in copy. No `hyphens: auto`.
- No display heading shipped without `text-wrap: balance`, no body paragraph without `text-wrap: pretty`.
- No generic centered hero on a blurred background image.
- No navbar with a colored background in the default state.
- No emoji in UI.
- No decorative dividers (wavy lines, illustrated separators).
- No component library used out of the box without restyling to this system (no default shadcn, no default Chakra).
- No more than two typeface families.
- No separate static font files where one variable file covers the range.
- No custom cursor. The system cursor is the cursor.
- No JavaScript positioning library for menus or tooltips where anchor positioning and the Popover API do the work.
- No AI filler copy ("dive into", "leverage", "utilize", "seamless", "robust", "innovative").

---

## Output expectation

Every component and page section should look like it belongs in a high end print magazine translated to the web, not assembled from a UI library. The grid breathes. The type is the hero when the photo is not, and it carries its hierarchy from one variable file. The lines are thin and intentional. The arrows are thin and directional. Nothing is round. Nothing is soft. Nothing is decorative.
